 "reading": [
  "Dolby's own validator accepts the authored master, so the ground truth is a valid Atmos programme and not a fixture only this decoder understands.",
  "Both codecs: all eight objects identified from their audio alone, so the encoder's spatial coding renumbering them does not matter.",
  "Both codecs: all seven static positions recovered exactly, error 0,0, at event offset 0 samples. That is the result the whole exercise was for -- the first object metadata this project has checked against authored numbers rather than against another decoder.",
  "The eighth object moves, and every authored position along its path comes back within 0,033 in room units, which is one position quantisation step. Its times do not: the encoder resamples the trajectory onto its own grid and shifts each authored position by 2 688 to 140 544 samples. That is an encoder property, reported separately, and the decoder faithfully reports what the encoder wrote.",
  "TrueHD and JOC agree on all of it, which is worth saying because the two carry objects in completely different ways: TrueHD as lossless channels, JOC as a parametric reconstruction from a five-channel downmix."
 ],
 "follow_up": [
  "Movement: authored trajectories with the encoder's resampling characterised rather than merely reported.",
  "Gain: authored steps at 0, -3, -6 and -12 dB and ramps between them.",
  "Size, divergence and distance: authored values against the quantisation the format allows.",
  "These need no new pipeline; the master, the encoders and the comparison all work."
 ]
